# What `docker build` never sends to the daemon: secrets, VCS, dependencies, and anything the image doesn't run.
# In the app: every image build reads it; the build context is the repo root.
# Used by: docker build (the Dockerfile here, and .github/workflows/publish-image.yml).
#
# Every file sent is a file a `COPY . .` can bake into a layer forever, so secrets and state go
# first. Add a project's own dirs (apps it doesn't ship, e2e suites, native projects) below.

# Secrets and infrastructure state: never in an image, even an intermediate stage.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform

# Version control and agent and editor config.
.git
.githooks
.github
.cursor
.claude
.gemini
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Dependencies and build output: the image installs and builds its own.
node_modules
.pnpm-store
coverage
dist

# Docs, plans, and infrastructure code: nothing at runtime reads them.
docs
infra
*.md
!README.md
# The agent guide is embedded in the binary (assets.go), so the Go build needs it.
!docs/agents-api.md
